 "observations": [
  "At 200 vehicles the proposed method's broadcast sent 26.4 \u00b1 1.4 frames per alert, 7.0 times fewer than blind flooding (185.8 \u00b1 0.3; its CH-to-CH route stage is a separate dissemination, counted in its own row); paired over the seeds the difference is -159.3 \u00b1 1.4 frames. <span class='src'>(summary.csv, paired.csv)</span>",
  "Against the strongest baseline, slotted 1-p + random delay (24.1 \u00b1 1.0 frames), the proposed method shows more frames than it at 200 vehicles (paired difference +2.3 \u00b1 1.6). <span class='src'>(summary.csv, paired.csv)</span>",
  "Receptions lost to collisions: 151 \u00b1 35 for the proposed method against 9632 \u00b1 208 for blind flooding and 188 \u00b1 55 for slotted 1-p + random delay (no significant difference than the latter: -36 \u00b1 55). <span class='src'>(summary.csv, paired.csv)</span>",
  "The proposed method reached 100 % of the reachable vehicles in every run at every density. Blind flooding reached 99.9 \u00b1 0.1 % and slotted 1-persistence 99.6 \u00b1 0.5 % at 200 vehicles. <span class='src'>(summary.csv)</span>",
  "Delay is the trade-off: the proposed method needed 35.3 \u00b1 1.8 ms to reach 90 % of the reachable vehicles against 31.8 \u00b1 1.1 ms for blind flooding (+3.5 \u00b1 1.7 ms paired; significantly slower). <span class='src'>(summary.csv, paired.csv)</span>",
  "First RSU registration took 21.4 \u00b1 1.9 ms with the proposed method and 22.0 \u00b1 1.9 ms with blind flooding (paired -0.6 \u00b1 1.0 ms: no significant difference); every scheme delivered to an RSU in 100 \u00b1 0 % of the runs. <span class='src'>(summary.csv, paired.csv)</span>",
  "The CH-to-CH route stage used 10.8 \u00b1 1.7 frames and lost no receptions, but by design it informs only the vehicles along and around the route (35.9 \u00b1 4.3 % reach) and delivered to the RSU in 93 \u00b1 9 % of the runs (it has no fallback). <span class='src'>(summary.csv)</span>",
  "With full protection no honest vehicle accepted a forged alert and no RSU registered one, at any density; without the reputation gate 13 %, 53 %, 87 %, 97 %, 97 %, 100 % of honest vehicles accepted it (50, 100, 200, 250, 300, 500 vehicles). <span class='src'>(forgery_summary.csv)</span>",
  "Against the strongest baseline, slotted 1-p + random delay, paired over the seeds at every density, the proposed method is mixed: frames on air worse at 100, 200 vehicles; receptions lost better at 250, 300, 500 vehicles; worse at 100 vehicles; reach better at 50, 100, 500 vehicles; time to 90 % better at 50 vehicles; worse at 300, 500 vehicles; first RSU registration worse at 50, 200, 300 vehicles (a density not named shows no significant difference). <span class='src'>(paired.csv)</span>",
  "In the comparison pairs, the proposed method's broadcast used fewer frames than the replayed baseline in 5 of 5 pairs (its CH-to-CH route stage is counted separately in the pair tables; single runs illustrate, the seeds above decide). <span class='src'>(pair records)</span>"
 ]
